{
  "id": "m6l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Capturar errores: try / except",
    "en": "Catching errors: try / except"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Cuando algo puede fallar"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Algunas operaciones pueden lanzar errores en ejecución (dividir entre cero, convertir texto no numérico…). Con `try`/`except` los **capturas** en lugar de que el programa se detenga."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "try:",
          "    n = int('hola')",
          "except ValueError:",
          "    print('no es un numero')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "no es un numero"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Puedes capturar un tipo concreto (`except ValueError:`) o varios. `else` se ejecuta si **no** hubo error, y `finally` se ejecuta **siempre**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "try:",
          "    x = 10 / 2",
          "except ZeroDivisionError:",
          "    print('div 0')",
          "else:",
          "    print('ok', x)",
          "finally:",
          "    print('fin')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ok 5.0",
          "fin"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Captura **solo** lo que esperas. Un `except:` que lo atrapa todo puede ocultar errores reales y dificultar la depuración."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "When something can fail"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Some operations can raise runtime errors (dividing by zero, converting non-numeric text…). With `try`/`except` you **catch** them instead of letting the program stop."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "try:",
          "    n = int('hola')",
          "except ValueError:",
          "    print('not a number')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "not a number"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "You can catch a specific type (`except ValueError:`) or several. `else` runs if there was **no** error, and `finally` runs **always**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "try:",
          "    x = 10 / 2",
          "except ZeroDivisionError:",
          "    print('div 0')",
          "else:",
          "    print('ok', x)",
          "finally:",
          "    print('fin')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ok 5.0",
          "fin"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Catch **only** what you expect. A bare `except:` can hide real bugs and make debugging harder."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m6l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `division_segura(a, b)` que devuelva `a / b`, o `None` si `b` es 0 (captura `ZeroDivisionError`).",
        "en": "Define `division_segura(a, b)` returning `a / b`, or `None` if `b` is 0 (catch `ZeroDivisionError`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def division_segura(a, b):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def division_segura(a, b):",
        "    try:",
        "        return a / b",
        "    except ZeroDivisionError:",
        "        return None"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Pon a / b dentro de un try.",
          "En el except devuelve None."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Put a / b inside a try.",
          "In the except, return None."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "division_segura",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                4,
                2
              ],
              "expected": 2.0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                1,
                0
              ],
              "expected": null
            },
            {
              "args": [
                9,
                3
              ],
              "expected": 3.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m6l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `a_entero(s)` que devuelva `int(s)`, o `-1` si `s` no representa un número (captura `ValueError`).",
        "en": "Define `a_entero(s)` returning `int(s)`, or `-1` if `s` is not a number (catch `ValueError`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def a_entero(s):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def a_entero(s):",
        "    try:",
        "        return int(s)",
        "    except ValueError:",
        "        return -1"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "int('hola') lanza ValueError.",
          "Captúralo y devuelve -1."
        ],
        "en": [
          "int('hola') raises ValueError.",
          "Catch it and return -1."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "a_entero",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "42"
              ],
              "expected": 42
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "hola"
              ],
              "expected": -1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "7"
              ],
              "expected": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}